---
title: Side-by-side columns
---

# Side-by-side columns

`\{% columns %}` places its children in equal-width columns, side by side.
Each column is either a list item (`*`) or a blank-line-separated block. The
`gap` attribute (points) sets the spacing, and `widths` (e.g. `widths="2 1"`
or `widths=[2, 1]`) makes them uneven. Render with `--assets-root examples`
so the swatch images resolve.

## Two images — list form

{% columns %}
* ![](swatch.png)
* ![](swatch.svg)
{% /columns %}

